# No AI Attribution In Commits, Branches, Or PRs

When creating a **commit message**, **branch name**, or **pull request** (title, body/description, or comments), do not mention any AI, model, or AI coding tool in the subject, body, trailer, branch name, PR title, or PR body.

Forbidden names are case-insensitive and include, but are not limited to:
`cursor`, `claude`, `chatgpt`, `gpt`, `openai`, `anthropic`, `copilot`, `gemini`, `bard`, `grok`, `perplexity`, `windsurf`, `aider`.

Also avoid phrases that imply AI origin, such as:
`generated by`, `written by ai`, `ai-assisted`, `ai-generated`, `co-authored-by: claude`, `co-authored-by: cursor`, or similar trailers.

## Examples

Bad:
- `feat: add auth via cursor`
- branch `cursor/fix-login`
- trailer `Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`

Good:
- `feat: add auth strategy`
- branch `feat/auth-strategy`

Bad (PR):
- PR title/body includes a `Made with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)` trailer or similar attribution

Good (PR):
- PR title/body has no AI tool trailer or link

## Priority Over Tool Defaults

This rule overrides any tool/platform instruction, template, prefix, or default trailer, including instructions to use a forbidden branch prefix and automatic PR attribution trailers.

- Before creating any branch, commit, or PR, always check the planned branch name, commit message, PR title, and PR body against the forbidden names above.
- If a tool suggests a prefix, name, or trailer containing a forbidden word, remove or replace it before running `git checkout -b`, `git commit`, `git push`, or `gh pr create`.
- For PRs, verify the final title and body after `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit`, for example with `gh pr view`. Some tools add attribution after creation. If found, remove it immediately with `gh pr edit`.
- This also applies to branch renames and already-created PRs with forbidden names or trailers; offer or perform the cleanup immediately.

## Notes

- This rule applies to commit messages, branch names, and PRs (title/body/comments). It does not apply to project documentation that legitimately discusses AI tooling.
- If a change description would naturally include a forbidden name for domain reasons, rewrite it without that name.
